cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OspreyDB: 1-Bit RaBitQ Indexing, DP Range Coalescing, and SIMD LUT-Rank Reranking"
message: "If you use OspreyDB in academic research or benchmarks, please cite this software using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ramos
    given-names: Lucas
  - name: "OspreyDB Contributors"
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ospreydb/ospreydb"
url: "https://ospreydb.dev"
abstract: >-
  OspreyDB is a 100% Apache-2.0 zero-copy vector database and CPU late-interaction
  reranking engine written in Rust for local disk and S3/object storage. It combines
  Fast Walsh-Hadamard Transform (FWHT) rotation, 1-Bit Binary K-Means clustering,
  asymmetric 1-bit RaBitQ scanning (.osi), TSP-ordered Zstd vector slabs accessed via
  O(k) Dynamic Programming range coalescing (RangePlanner, .osv), and 2-bit nested-lattice
  SIMD lookup-table ColBERT MaxSim reranking (LUT-Rank, .osr).
keywords:
  - vector-search
  - rabitq
  - range-planner
  - lut-rank
  - colbert
  - simd
  - object-storage
  - rust
